# Reflection

### Which framework was strongest?

The EU AI Act received the lowest score at 4/20 because it includes specific legal requirements that the organisation has not yet addressed.

ISO 42001 and NIST AI RMF both scored 5/20. The organisation received some credit because it already has general policies and some knowledge of its AI systems, but these practices are not yet part of a formal AI governance program.

### Where is the largest governance gap?

The biggest gap is the resume screening model.

It may be considered a high risk AI system under the EU AI Act, but there are currently no proper controls in place. There is also no bias testing, technical documentation, or clear risk management process for the model.

### What is one action in the next 30 days?

The first priority should be to appoint one person who is clearly responsible for AI governance and risk.

Having a clear owner will make it easier to coordinate the risk assessment, involve the right teams, and start addressing the other gaps identified in this assessment.
